.TH GFXSTRESS 1
.SH NAME
gfxstress \- deterministic Draw/draw3d graphics stress test
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/gfxstress
.RI [ phase
.RI [ seconds ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Gfxstress
is a deterministic, phase-oriented exerciser for the Draw protocol,
memdraw, screen damage/upload, and the optional
.IR draw3d (2)
device path. Each phase drives a different mix of operations (plain
fills, straight copies, overlapping regions, alpha blending, masked
draws) at a fixed, seeded pattern, so a run can be compared frame for
frame against a previous one rather than relying on eyeballing it.
.PP
.B thickellipse
is not a performance phase but a regression test, and the one phase here
that is an oracle: it draws ellipses at the four semithicknesses for
which
.IR memellipse 's
brush disc used to be allocated too small, and a run that reaches its
.B GFXSTRESS
line at all is the check passing.
.PP
.IR memellipse (2)
sends any large semithickness into its brushed-with-circles path, which
allocates the brush disc as a
.B GREY1
.BR Rect(\-t,\-t,t+1,t+1) .
.IR allocmemimage (2)
sized that with
.B nw = l*Dy(r)
in
.BR u32 ,
so a thickness whose true word count passed 2\u32\d wrapped to a small
one: at
.B t=185352
the pool returned 83352 bytes for a rectangle holding 17.2 GB of pixels,
and the fill done next walked off the end of it.
.IR draw (3)
rejects a negative semidiameter and a negative thickness but bounds none
of them above, so the value arrives from the wire unchallenged.
.PP
With no arguments it cycles through all phases; giving
.I phase
restricts the run to that one, and
.I seconds
bounds how long it runs \(em useful for exact placement in automated
testing, where waiting for a pointer-driven placement would make the
run non-deterministic.
.SH BUGS
The phases are an exerciser, not an oracle: nothing here checks the
pixels, so a phase proves that a path was
.B taken
and says nothing about whether it was taken correctly.
.PP
.B thickellipse
covers only the thicknesses at which the word count wraps, which it
finds by arithmetic rather than by search. A thickness large enough to
be refused outright, or large enough to overflow
.IR memellipse 's
own
.B (t<<1)*(a\-b)
criterion before the allocator is ever reached, is not exercised.
.PP
Nothing here reaches the brush-disc path with a thickness small enough
to be ordinary, which is the case that matters most: the
.B ellipse
phase does reach it \(em at
.BR t=2 ,
.B 2t(a\-b) > b\u2\d
holds for most of its radii, so the brushed path is the common case
there and not the exception \(em but it reaches it incidentally, and
nothing in the name or the code says so.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/gfxstress.b
